  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Integrated GBV-SRH response to mitigate cyclone induced risks on women, girls, and third gender including pregnant women and persons with disability</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main goal of this project is to provide sexual and reproductive health (SRH) assistance and protection against Gender Based Violence (GBV) to vulnerable women and girls in the coastal districts of Bangladesh. This UNFPA project provides inter-agency emergency reproductive health kits and deploy midwives and community volunteers to support pregnant women. Along with the kits, pregnant women receive cash support to cover transport to health facilities, referral to obstetric emergencies, and encourage facility-based delivery. This project targets a total of 3,120 women and girls, 80 men and 100 people with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
